nnected_server_and_client_memory\n```\n\nHmm, in mcp 2.x there's `mcp.shared_memory.create_connected_server_and_client_memory` or FastMCP `.run()`... Let me check what's available in mcp 2.1.1. There's `mcp.client.stdio` for subprocess transport, and `Client` context manager in `mcp` top-level: `from mcp import Client; from mcp.client.streamable_http import ...`. For testing FastMCP servers, common recipe:\n\n```python\nimport anyio\nfrom mcp import Client\nfrom mcp.shared_memory import create_connected_server_and_client_memory\n\nasync def test():\n    async with create_connected_memory(...) \n```\n\nLet me check the mcp package contents at implementation time. Alternative robust approach: launch `server.py` as subprocess with `mcp.client.stdio.stdio_client` and `ClientSession` — full end-to-end test. That works with any version. I'll write one test that spawns the server subprocess, lists tools, calls `search_matches` and `head_to_head`. Plus unit tests of the query layer directly.\n\nWait — mcp 2.1.1 might have the new `Client`/`ServerSession` API. I'll check the installed package API before writing the test.\n\nrequirements.txt: mcp>=2.0. Plus pytest for dev.\n\nPython version: 3.12. Use modern typing.\n\nLet me now verify the dedup overlap question and the \"Athletico\" bare team question.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d945cd6001CjpUToHQ23Fk6x","sessionID":"ses_fa26ff80dffeDQKLW66czjBP2c","messageID":"msg_05d9382210016CpR424qZJlRRN"}}
