onto the primary record by (season, home_key, away_key) — good.\n\nHowever cross-file questions like \"What competitions has Palmeiras played in?\" need all competitions — with primary-source policy, Palmeiras matches come from: Brasileirão (Brasileirao file), Copa do Brasil (Cup file), Libertadores (Lib file), BR-Football (Serie A 2023 only for Palmeiras... wait Palmeiras in 2023 Serie A — yes BR-Football covers 2023). Plus BR-Football Serie A 2014-2023 would be dropped for 2014-2022 (dup of primary). OK.\n\nBut wait — is the Brasileirao_Matches file complete for 2012-2022? 4180 = 11 seasons × 380. Yes, complete.\n\nHistorical 2003-2019: 6886 matches. Serie A: 2003-2005 had 24 teams (468/season?)... 2003: 549? Whatever — it covers 2003-2011 for our primary policy.\n\nBR-Football Serie B and Serie C — no other source, fine.\n\nCopa do Brasil: Cup file 2012-2021 (1337 matches); BR-Football \"Copa do Brasil\" 2014-2023 (1123). Primary: Cup file 2012-2021; BR-Football fills 2022-2023. Wait but do the two files' Copa do Brasil dates align? Doesn't matter with the policy.\n\nHmm, but there's a subtlety: Cup file rounds — 2021 data ends at round 4?? 2021: rounds 1,2,3(32),4(16) — that's incomplete! 2021 Copa do Brasil had more rounds (final between Athletico-PR? no — 2021 final: Atlético-MG x Athletico-PR... hmm actually the 2021 Copa do Brasil was won by Atlético Mineiro, final vs Athletico-PR). The file only has 108 matches for 2021 (40+20+32+16=108). The real tournament had 2021: 91 matches? Whatever — it's the provided data. And BR-Football has Copa do Brasil 2021-2023 too. Hmm wait — BR-Football Copa do Brasil: 1123 matches 2014-2023. The two overlap 2014-2021. For 2021, Cup file has rounds 1-4 (108 matches) while BR-Football might have the complete 2021 Copa do Brasil. Tricky. Policy refinement per competition+season:\n- Copa do Brasil season coverage: if season in Cup file seasons AND Cup file has ≥ 100 matches for that season → use Cup file, else BR-Football. Hmm,