astMCP OK\")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"FastMCP fail:\", e)\nimport mcp.client.stdio as s\nprint(\"stdio:\", [n for n in dir(s) if not n.startswith('_')])\ntry:\n    import mcp.shared_memory as sm\n    print(\"shared_memory:\", [n for n in dir(sm) if not n.startswith('_')])\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"no shared_memory:\", e)\nEOF","time":{"start":1788276622353,"end":1788276622403}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Data quirks to handle:\n- Lib: 2 rows with '-' goals and 'NA' datetime (2021 unfinished round-of-16 Boca-River; the Flamengo-Athletico final with NA season — actually the 2022 final Flamengo 1-0 Athletico). Handle: goals None, date None → keep but mark as unplayed/unknown.\n- Cup: 16 rows with 'NA' goals (2021 round 4+ matches not played/recorded) — keep with None goals, exclude from stats.\n- FIFA: Position can be '' (60 players). Club can be empty.\n\nNow I have everything needed. Let me design and write the code.\n\n**Project structure:**\n\n```\nserver.py                       # MCP server entry point\nbrazilian_soccer/\n    __init__.py\n    normalize.py                # team-name canonicalization\n    dates.py                    # date parsing\n    models.py                   # Match, Player dataclasses\n    data.py                     # SoccerData: load all 6 CSVs, unified primary match set + extended stats\n    queries.py                  # query layer used by MCP tools\nrequirements.txt\ntests/\n    conftest.py\n    test_normalize.py\n    test_match_queries.py\n    test_team_queries.py\n    test_player_queries.py\n    test_competition_queries.py\n    test_statistics.py\n    test_mcp_server.py\nREADME.md                       # updated\n```\n\n**normalize.py** design:\n\n```python\nBRAZILIAN_UFS = {...27 codes...}\nCOUNTRY_CODES = {'URU','ARG','EQU','PAR','PER','VEN','COL','CHI','BOL','MEX','USA','JPN'}\nLEGAL_TOKENS = {'ec','sc','fc','ac','cb','aa','cbd','esporte','esportiva','clube','club','futebol','regatas','de','do','da','dos','das','the'}\n\nAMBIGUOUS_BASES = {\n  'atletico': {'MG': 'atletico-mg', 'GO': 'atletico-go', 'PR': 'athletico-pr'},\n  'america': {'MG': 'america-mg', 'RN': 'america-rn', 'SC': 'america-sc'},\n  'botafogo': {'RJ': 'botafogo', 'PB': 'botafogo-pb', 'SP': 'botafogo-sp'},\n  ...maybe others discovered empirically\n}\nALIASES = {\n  'atletico mineiro': 'atletico-mg',\n  'atlético mineiro' (folded: 'atletico mineiro'),\n  'atletico paranaense': 'athletico-pr',\n  'athletico paranaense': 'athletico-pr',\n  'athletico': 'athletico-pr',\n  'paranaense': 'athletico-pr',\n  'ceara sporting': 'ceara',\n  'sport recife': 'sport',\n  'vasco gama': 'vasco',\n  'spfc': 'sao paulo',\n  'america fc': 'america-mg',   # from FIFA \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → paren dropped → 'america fc' → tokens minus fc → 'america' → then alias 'america' → 'america-mg'\n  'america': 'america-mg',\n  'botafogo': 'botafogo',  (identity)\n  'internacional': 'internacional',\n  'gremio': 'gremio',\n  'corinthians paulista'?... skip\n}\n```\n\nWait — 'america' → 'america-mg' as an alias is context-dependent (FIFA). But in match data, \"América-RN\" keeps uf so base never appears bare from match files. Bare 'america' only arises from FIFA club. So alias is safe.\n\nAlso 'botafogo' ambiguous in BR-Football? Let me check if \"Botafogo PB\" appears in BR-Football (Serie C). I'll check when I run the collision report and add to AMBIGUOUS_BASES accordingly. With AMBIGUOUS_BASES['botafogo'] = {'RJ':'botafogo','PB':'botafogo-pb'}, bare 'botafogo' (no uf) → default alias 'botafogo' (RJ). In code: AMBIGUOUS resolution needs uf; if uf missing → look in DEFAULT for base or return base itself.\n\nActually let me restructure the resolution algorithm cleanly:\n\n```python\ndef team_key(raw: str) -> str:\n    s = strip parentheticals (but retain country-code parentheticals as suffix tokens)\n    s = fold accents → ascii\n    tokens = split non-alnum\n    if len(tokens) > 1 and tokens[-1] in (UFs | COUNTRY_CODES): code = tokens.pop()\n    tokens = [t for t in tokens if t not in LEGAL_TOKENS]\n    base = ' '.join(tokens)\n    # resolve aliases on base (before uf resolution? both orders)\n    if code in COUNTRY_CODES: return f\"{base}-{code.lower()}\"  # foreign teams keep code\n    # Brazilian UF or no code:\n    if base in AMBIGUOUS:\n        if code: return AMBIGUOUS[base].get(code, f\"{base}-{code.lower()}\")\n        return BARE_DEFAULT.get(base, base)   # e.g. 'atletico' bare → ? 'athletico' bare → 'athletico-pr'\n    if base in ALIASES: return ALIASES[base]\n    return base\n```\n\nHmm wait, order matters: \"Atletico Mineiro\" → tokens [atletico, mineiro], no trailing code → base \"atletico mineiro\" → not ambiguous → ALIASES['atletico mineiro'] = 'atletico-mg' ✓.\n\"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → paren \"Minas Gerais\" not a code → dropped → tokens [america, fc] → no trailing code → strip fc → base \"america\" → AMBIGUOUS? 'america' in AMBIGUOUS with no code → BARE_DEFAULT['america'] = 'america-mg' ✓.\n\"Atlético Paranaense\" → base \"atletico paranaense\" → ALIASES → 'athletico-pr' ✓.\n\"Athletico-PR\" → tokens [athletico, pr] → pr is UF → code PR → tokens [athletico] → base 'athletico' → AMBIGUOUS? I'll add 'athletico': {'PR': 'athletico-pr'} and BARE_DEFAULT['athletico'] = 'athletico-pr'. ✓\n\"Atletico-PR\" → code PR, base 'atletico' → AMBIGUOUS['atletico']['PR'] = 'athletico-pr' ✓.\n\"Atlético-MG\" → 'atletico-mg' ✓.\n\"Botafogo-RJ\" → base 'botafogo' code RJ → AMBIGUOUS['botafogo']['RJ'] = 'botafogo' ✓. \"Botafogo PB\" → 'botafogo-pb' ✓. Bare \"Botafogo\" (FIFA) → BARE_DEFAULT['botafogo'] = 'botafogo' ✓.\n\"Guaraní-PAR\" → code PAR (country) → \"guarani-par\" ✓ distinct from \"Guarani\" ✓. \"Guaraní (PAR)\" → paren content PAR is country code → retained as token → tokens [guarani, par] → code PAR → 'guarani-par' ✓.\n\"Nacional (URU)\" → 'nacional-uru' ✓; \"Nacional-URU\" ✓; \"Nacional (PAR)\" → 'nacional-par' ✓.\n\"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" → tokens [vasco, da, gama, rj] → code RJ → strip da → base 'vasco gama' → ALIASES['vasco gama'] = 'vasco' ✓. Bare \"Vasco\" → 'vasco' ✓.\n\"São Paulo-SP\" → code SP, base 'sao paulo' → not ambiguous → 'sao paulo' ✓. \"SPFC\" → lower 'spfc' → ALIASES → 'sao paulo' ✓.\n\"Sport Club do Recife\" → tokens [sport, club→strip? 'club' in LEGAL? I have 'club' in LEGAL_TOKENS → [sport, do→strip, recife] → base 'sport recife' → ALIASES['sport recife'] = 'sport' ✓. \"Sport-PE\" → base 'sport' code PE → 'sport' not ambiguous → 'sport' ✓ (UF dropped). \n\"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\" → paren dropped → tokens [boavista, sport, club→strip, rj] → code RJ → base 'boavista sport' → 'boavista sport' key. Meh — unique, fine. Hmm wait 'sport' remains: \"Boavista Sport\" — fine, distinct key.\n\"Ceará Sporting Club\" → tokens [ceara, sporting, club→strip] → 'ceara sporting' → ALIASES → 'ceara' ✓. \"Ceara-CE\" → base 'ceara' → 'ceara' ✓.\n\"EC Bahia\" → 'bahia' ✓.\n\"Fortaleza FC\" → 'fortaleza' ✓.\n\"America MG\" → code MG → AMBIGUOUS → 'america-mg' ✓.\n\"Atlético-MG\" → 'atletico-mg' ✓.\n\"Juventude-RS\" → 'juventude' ✓.\n\"Paraná-PR\" → 'parana' — hmm \"Paraná\" base unambiguous? FIFA \"Paraná\", historical \"Parana-PR\" → all 'parana' ✓.\n\"Red Bull Bragantino-SP\" → base 'red bull bragantino' ✓.\n\"Coritiba-PR\" → 'coritiba' ✓.\n\"Goiás-GO\" → 'goias' ✓.\n\"Chapecoense-SC\" → 'chapecoense' ✓.\n\"CRB\"? not in data? fine.\n\"CSA\" → 'csa' ✓.\n\"Cuiaba-MT\" → 'cuiaba' ✓.\n\"Internacional-RS\" → 'internacional' — wait, is 'internacional' ambiguous with foreign clubs? Libertadores \"Internacional\" (Brazilian) only. Ecuador's \"Independiente del Valle\" etc. distinct. OK.\n\nForeign: \"Barcelona-EQU\" → code EQU (country) → 'barcelona-equ' ✓ (distinct from FC Barcelona in FIFA! FIFA \"FC Barcelona\" → tokens [fc→strip, barcelona] → 'barcelona' ✓ different key — good, they ARE different clubs).\n\n\"River Plate-URU\" → 'river plate uru'?? code URU