{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788276638233,"sessionID":"ses_fa26ff80dffeDQKLW66czjBP2c","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-88e5b0f18c755337","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport inspect\nfrom mcp.server.mcpserver import MCPServer\nprint(\"run:\", inspect.signature(MCPServer.run))\nprint(\"run_stdio_async:\", inspect.signature(MCPServer.run_stdio_async))\nfrom mcp import Client, ClientSession\nprint(\"Client init:\", inspect.signature(Client.__init__))\nfrom mcp.client.stdio import stdio_client, StdioServerParameters\nprint(\"stdio_client:\", inspect.signature(stdio_client))\nprint(\"call_tool:\", inspect.signature(ClientSession.call_tool))\nimport mcp.types as t\nprint([n for n in dir(t) if 'Error' in n or 'MCPError' in n][:10])\nfrom mcp import MCPError\nprint(\"MCPError ok\")\nEOF"},"output":"run: (self, transport: \"Literal['stdio', 'sse', 'streamable-http']\" = 'stdio', **kwargs: 'Any') -> 'None'\nrun_stdio_async: (self) -> 'None'\nClient init: (self, server: 'Server[Any] | MCPServer | Transport | StdioServerParameters | str', *, raise_exceptions: 'bool' = False, read_timeout_seconds: 'float | None' = None, sampling_callback: 'SamplingFnT | None' = None, sampling_capabilities: 'types.SamplingCapability | None' = None, list_roots_callback: 'ListRootsFnT | None' = None, logging_callback: 'LoggingFnT | None' = None, log_level: 'LoggingLevel | None' = None, message_handler: 'MessageHandlerFnT | None' = None, client_info: 'Implementation | None' = None, mode: 'ConnectMode' = 'auto', prior_discover: 'types.DiscoverResult | None' = None, elicitation_callback: 'ElicitationFnT | None' = None, input_required_max_rounds: 'int' = 10, extensions: 'Sequence[ClientExtension] | None' = None, cache: 'CacheConfig | None' = <factory>) -> None\nstdio_client: (server: mcp.client.stdio.StdioServerParameters, errlog: <class 'TextIO'> = <_io.TextIOWrapper name='<stderr>' mode='w' encoding='utf-8'>) -> collections.abc.AsyncGenerator[tuple[mcp.shared._stream_protocols.ReadStream[mcp.shared.message.SessionMessage | Exception], mcp.shared._stream_protocols.WriteStream[mcp.shared.message.SessionMessage]], None]\ncall_tool: (self, name: 'str', arguments: 'dict[str, Any] | None' = None, read_timeout_seconds: 'float | None' = None, progress_callback: 'ProgressFnT | None' = None, *, input_responses: 'types.InputResponses | None' = None, request_state: 'str | None' = None, meta: 'RequestParamsMeta | None' = None, allow_input_required: 'bool' = False, allow_claimed: 'bool' = False) -> 'types.CallToolResult | types.InputRequiredResult | types.Result'\n['ElicitationRequiredErrorData', 'ErrorData', 'JSONRPCError', 'MissingRequiredClientCapabilityErrorData', 'UnsupportedProtocolVersionErrorData']\nMCPError ok\n","metadata":{"output":"run: (self, transport: \"Literal['stdio', 'sse', 'streamable-http']\" = 'stdio', **kwargs: 'Any') -> 'None'\nrun_stdio_async: (self) -> 'None'\nClient init: (self, server: 'Server[Any] | MCPServer | Transport | StdioServerParameters | str', *, raise_exceptions: 'bool' = False, read_timeout_seconds: 'float | None' = None, sampling_callback: 'SamplingFnT | None' = None, sampling_capabilities: 'types.SamplingCapability | None' = None, list_roots_callback: 'ListRootsFnT | None' = None, logging_callback: 'LoggingFnT | None' = None, log_level: 'LoggingLevel | None' = None, message_handler: 'MessageHandlerFnT | None' = None, client_info: 'Implementation | None' = None, mode: 'ConnectMode' = 'auto', prior_discover: 'types.DiscoverResult | None' = None, elicitation_callback: 'ElicitationFnT | None' = None, input_required_max_rounds: 'int' = 10, extensions: 'Sequence[ClientExtension] | None' = None, cache: 'CacheConfig | None' = <factory>) -> None\nstdio_client: (server: mcp.client.stdio.StdioServerParameters, errlog: <class 'TextIO'> = <_io.TextIOWrapper name='<stderr>' mode='w' encoding='utf-8'>) -> collections.abc.AsyncGenerator[tuple[mcp.shared._stream_protocols.ReadStream[mcp.shared.message.SessionMessage | Exception], mcp.shared._stream_protocols.WriteStream[mcp.shared.message.SessionMessage]], None]\ncall_tool: (self, name: 'str', arguments: 'dict[str, Any] | None' = None, read_timeout_seconds: 'float | None' = None, progress_callback: 'ProgressFnT | None' = None, *, input_responses: 'types.InputResponses | None' = None, request_state: 'str | None' = None, meta: 'RequestParamsMeta | None' = None, allow_input_required: 'bool' = False, allow_claimed: 'bool' = False) -> 'types.CallToolResult | types.InputRequiredResult | types.Result'\n['ElicitationRequiredErrorData', 'ErrorData', 'JSONRPCError', 'MissingRequiredClientCapabilityErrorData', 'UnsupportedProtocolVersionErrorData']\nMCPError ok\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport inspect\nfrom mcp.server.mcpserver import MCPServer\nprint(\"run:\", inspect.signature(MCPServer.run))\nprint(\"run_stdio_async:\", inspect.signature(MCPServer.run_stdio_async))\nfrom mcp import Client, ClientSession\nprint(\"Client init:\", inspect.signature(Client.__init__))\nfrom mcp.client.stdio import stdio_client, StdioServerParameters\nprint(\"stdio_client:\", inspect.signature(stdio_client))\nprint(\"call_tool:\", inspect.signature(ClientSession.call_tool))\nimport mcp.types as t\nprint([n for n in dir(t) if 'Error' in n or 'MCPError' in n][:10])\nfrom mcp import MCPError\nprint(\"MCPError ok\")\nEOF","time":{"start":1788276638185,"end":1788276638231}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The MCP 2.x API: `from mcp.server.mcpserver import MCPServer`, `@server.tool()` decorator, `server.run()` for stdio. Client: `from mcp import Client, StdioServerParameters` + `from mcp.client.stdio import stdio_client`. Also `ClientSession` from `mcp` top-level. Result fields snake_case (`is_error`, `structured_content`, `input_schema`).\n\nKey details from migration guide:\n- `MCPServer.tool()` decorator with `name`, `description`? The signature shows `tool(name=None, title=None, description=None, annotations=None, ...)` — wait, the signature printed was: `(self, name=None, title=None, description=None, annotations=None, icons=None, meta=None, structured_output=None)`. Good — so `@mcp.tool()` works like FastMCP, inferring from docstring/type hints.\n- `MCPError` raised from a handler surfaces as JSON-RPC error. For tool errors, I can raise MCPError or return error text. I'll return error dicts as normal results (friendlier for tests).\n- Server handler results validated against protocol schema — return types must be serializable (dict/list/str fine).\n\nLet me check how `MCPServer.run()` is invoked for stdio: `run()` — in v2, `run()` without args defaults to stdio? The dir listing shows `run`, `run_stdio_async`, `run_streamable_http_async`, `run_sse_async`. In v1 FastMCP, `run()` took a transport arg. In v2 \"Transport-specific parameters moved from MCPServer constructor to run()/app methods\". Let me check the signature of `run()`.\n\nAlso check how the Client + stdio_client works for the test. Let me look at a minimal example from the docs — get-started first steps page. Let me fetch a small portion... Actually simpler: introspect signatures directly","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d97fcea001yEo1tKL1IK5JAq","sessionID":"ses_fa26ff80dffeDQKLW66czjBP2c","messageID":"msg_05d97e4de001EsAuwdNDNJUmNA"}}
