{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788276725514,"sessionID":"ses_fa26ff80dffeDQKLW66czjBP2c","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"todowrite","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a91d7a6daa267c27","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"todos":[{"content":"Implement brazilian_soccer package (normalize, dates, models, data, queries)","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run team-name collision report and verify data facts for test assertions","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement server.py MCP server (MCPServer, stdio)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write BDD GWT pytest suite (unit + MCP end-to-end)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run full test suite, lint, fix issues","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Update README.md with usage and tool catalog","status":"pending","priority":"medium"}]},"output":"[\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Implement brazilian_soccer package (normalize, dates, models, data, queries)\",\n    \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Run team-name collision report and verify data facts for test assertions\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Implement server.py MCP server (MCPServer, stdio)\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Write BDD GWT pytest suite (unit + MCP end-to-end)\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Run full test suite, lint, fix issues\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Update README.md with usage and tool catalog\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"medium\"\n  }\n]","metadata":{"todos":[{"content":"Implement brazilian_soccer package (normalize, dates, models, data, queries)","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run team-name collision report and verify data facts for test assertions","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement server.py MCP server (MCPServer, stdio)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write BDD GWT pytest suite (unit + MCP end-to-end)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run full test suite, lint, fix issues","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Update README.md with usage and tool catalog","status":"pending","priority":"medium"}],"truncated":false},"title":"6 todos","time":{"start":1788276725509,"end":1788276725511}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The v2 API is clear now:\n- Server: `MCPServer(name=..., ...)` + `@server.tool()` decorator + `server.run()` (stdio default).\n- Client (v2 style): `Client(StdioServerParameters(...))` — the new `Client` class accepts a server directly and is an async context manager. That's much simpler than manual stdio_client + ClientSession. `async with Client(params) as client: result = await client.call_tool(...)`.\n\nLet me now write all the code. Structure:\n\n```\nserver.py                       # MCP server entry\nbrazilian_soccer/\n    __init__.py\n    normalize.py\n    dates.py\n    models.py\n    data.py\n    queries.py\nrequirements.txt\ntests/\n    conftest.py\n    test_normalize.py\n    test_dates.py (fold into test_normalize? separate small file fine)\n    test_match_queries.py\n    test_team_queries.py\n    test_player_queries.py\n    test_competition_queries.py\n    test_statistics.py\n    test_mcp_server.py\nREADME.md update\n```\n\nLet me write each module carefully.\n\n### normalize.py\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\nimport re\nimport unicodedata\n\nBRAZILIAN_UFS = {...}\nCOUNTRY_CODES = {...}\n_LEGAL_TOKENS = {...}\n\nAMBIGUOUS_BASES: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = {\n    \"atletico\": {\"MG\": \"atletico-mg\", \"GO\": \"atletico-go\", \"PR\": \"athletico-pr\"},\n    \"athletico\": {\"PR\": \"athletico-pr\"},\n    \"america\": {\"MG\": \"america-mg\", \"RN\": \"america-rn\", \"SC\": \"america-sc\"},\n    \"botafogo\": {\"RJ\": \"botafogo\", \"PB\": \"botafogo-pb\", \"SP\": \"botafogo-sp\"},\n    \"nacional\": ...? no—handled via country codes\n}\n\nBARE_ALIASES = {\n    \"america\": \"america-mg\",\n    \"athletico\": \"athletico-pr\",\n    \"botafogo\": \"botafogo\",   # identity, fine to omit\n}\n\nALIASES = {\n    \"atletico mineiro\": \"atletico-mg\",\n    \"atletico paranaense\": \"athletico-pr\",\n    \"athletico paranaense\": \"athletico-pr\",\n    \"paranaense\": \"athletico-pr\",\n    \"ceara sporting\": \"ceara\",\n    \"sport recife\": \"sport\",\n    \"vasco gama\": \"vasco\",\n    \"spfc\": \"sao paulo\",\n    \"corinthians paulista\": \"corinthians\",\n    \"socio esportiva palmeiras\"? not needed\n    \"clube regatas flamengo\"? not needed\n}\n```\n\nWait — one more: FIFA \"Bahia\" → 'bahia' ✓. \"Esporte Clube Bahia\"? not present. BR-Football \"EC Bahia\" ✓.\n\nWhat about \"Atlético-GO\" appearing as \"Atletico-GO\" in Brasileirao file → base 'atletico' + GO → 'atletico-go' ✓.\n\n\"Guarani\" SP vs... fine.\n\nAlso historical \"América-RN\" → 'america-rn' ✓; historical \"América-MG\" → 'america-mg' ✓; BR-Football \"America MG\" → 'america-mg' ✓.\n\nWhat about trailing UF inside a longer name where UF is a real word? E.g. \"Peñarol\"? no. UF codes are 2 letters uppercase; after fold+lowercase I lose case! \"America MG\" → tokens [america, mg] both lowercase — 'mg' in UF set → treated as UF. But what about a team like... \"ABC-RN\"? 'abc' fine. Any name ENDING with a token that's a UF code but actually part of name? e.g. \"Goias-GO\" → 'goias' + GO ✓ correct. \"Ceara-CE\" ✓. \"Sport-PE\" ✓. \"Santos-SP\"? \"Santos-SP\" → 'santos' ✓. Names ending in lowercase 'sp'/'rj' as real words — none plausible. OK.\n\nBUT careful: case is lost — \"Santos Laguna\" doesn't end in UF. \"Palmeiras-SP\" ✓. What about Brazilian names in BR-Football like \"Botafogo RJ\" → [botafogo, rj] → UF ✓. \"Vila Nova-GO\"? \"Vila Nova FC\"? BR-Football Serie B \"Vila Nova-GO\"? would → 'vila nova' ✓ good.\n\nEdge: \"Athletico\" bare (Libertadores) → 'athletico' → BARE_ALIASES → 'athletico-pr' ✓.\n\nEdge: \"Real Atlético\" → [real, atletico] → 'real atletico' — trailing token 'atletico' not a code ✓.\n\nEdge: \"Atlético Tucumán\" → 'atletico tucuman' ✓ distinct from 'atletico-mg'.\n\nEdge: FIFA \"Club Atlético Aldosivi\" → tokens [club→strip? 'club' in LEGAL_TOKENS, atletico, aldosivi] → 'atletico aldosivi' ✓.\n\nEdge: \"Independiente del Valle\" → 'del' stripped → 'independiente valle'; also \"Ind. Santa Fe\" → 'ind santa fe'? 'ind' stays. OK distinct.\n\nEdge: \"O'Higgins\" → split on non-alnum → ['o','higgins'] → 'o higgins' ✓ consistent.\n\nEdge: \"Colo-Colo\" → 'colo colo' ✓.\n\nEdge: \"Deportivo Táchira\" → 'deportivo tachira' ✓.\n\nEdge: \"Junior de Barranquilla\" → [junior, de→strip, barranquilla] → 'junior barranquilla'; also plain \"Junior\"? If \"Junior\" appears alone elsewhere (Colombian club \"Junior\" in FIFA? \"Junior\" appears as \"Junior de Barranquilla\" in lib; FIFA might have \"Junior\"? FIFA Colombian clubs: \"Deportes Tolima\", \"Independiente Medellín\", \"Atlético Nacional\", \"Once Caldas\"... maybe \"Junior\" exists). Two different keys for possibly same club — only matters if user queries; acceptable. Actually add alias \"junior\" → \"junior barranquilla\"? Hmm — if FIFA has \"Junior\" it's the Colombian club, same as lib's. I'll add the alias if FIFA has bare \"Junior\". Let me check later in collision report.\n\nEdge: FIFA \"Grêmio\" → 'gremio' matches \"Gremio-RS\" → base 'gremio' ✓ same key ✓.\n\nEdge: FIFA \"Atlético Mineiro\" → 'atletico mineiro' → ALIASES → 'atletico-mg' ✓. FIFA \"Cruzeiro\" → 'cruzeiro' ✓. FIFA \"Santos\" → 'santos' ✓. FIFA \"Fluminense\" ✓. FIFA \"Internacional\" ✓. FIFA \"Chapecoense\" ✓. FIFA \"Bahia\" ✓. FIFA \"Paraná\" → 'parana' ✓ matches \"Parana-PR\" → 'parana' ✓. FIFA \"Vitória\" → 'vitoria' ✓. FIFA \"Ceará Sporting Club\" → 'ceara sporting' → ALIASES → 'ceara' ✓. FIFA \"Sport Club do Recife\" → [sport, club→strip, do→strip, recife] → 'sport recife' → ALIASES → 'sport' ✓ matches \"Sport-PE\" ✓. FIFA \"Atlético Paranaense\" → 'atletico paranaense' → 'athletico-pr' ✓. FIFA \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → paren '(Minas Gerais)' — content not a code → dropped → 'america fc' → strip fc → 'america' → AMBIGUOUS base, no UF → BARE_ALIASES['america'] = 'america-mg' ✓. FIFA \"Botafogo\" → BARE → 'botafogo' (RJ) ✓. \n\nEdge: \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\" → paren dropped → [boavista, sport, club→strip, rj] → base 'boavista sport' + uf RJ → 'boavosta sport'... 'boavista sport' unambiguous → key 'boavista sport' ✓ fine.\n\nNow — subtle: my algorithm strips LEGAL_TOKENS BEFORE checking trailing UF? Order: split → check trailing code FIRST (on raw token list before legal stripping, since codes are pure tokens like 'rj') — e.g. \"Vasco da Gama-RJ\" → [vasco, da, gama, rj] → trailing 'rj' is UF → pop → [vasco, da, gama] → strip legals ('da') → 'vasco gama' → alias → 'vasco' ✓.\n\nBut what if name ends with legal token after code? \"América FC\"? → [america, fc] → no trailing code → strip fc → 'america' → BARE ✓.\n\nWhat about names ending with UF that is ALSO a legal-ish? No overlap.\n\nOne more: \"Criciúma - SC\" (Cup file, spaced hyphen) → [criciuma, sc] → 'sc' is UF ✓ → 'criciuma' ✓. And 'sc' also in LEGAL_TOKENS — but code-check happens before legal-strip, so it's popped as UF ✓. But what about \"SC Corinthians\"? (form \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\"?) — if a name is \"SC Internacional\" → [sc, internacional] — leading 'sc' stripped as legal ✓ fine.\n\nEdge: name that IS just a legal token? None.\n\nEdge: \"EC Vitória\" → 'vitoria' ✓. \"EC São José\"? fine.\n\nEdge: trailing code with lowercase input where code equals a word: \"Sport Boys\" (Peru) → [sport, boys] ✓ no code. \"The Strongest\" → 'the' stripped → 'strongest' ✓. \"Always Ready\" ✓.\n\nEdge: \"Universidad Católica\" ✓.\n\nEdge: 3-letter country codes trailing: \"Barcelona-EQU\" → [barcelona, equ] → 'equ' in COUNTRY_CODES → key 'barcelona-equ' ✓. \"LDU\" — single token, len 3, but check requires len(tokens)>1 ✓ 'ldu' stays.\n\nEdge: what about \"Palmeiras-SP\" vs \"Palmeiras\"? Both → 'palmeiras' ✓ (uf dropped since unambiguous).\n\nEdge: \"Náutico-PE\"/\"Nautico-PE\"/\"Náutico\" → 'nautico' ✓.\n\nEdge: \"Flamengo-RJ\"/\"Flamengo\"/\"Clube de Regatas do Flamengo\" → 'flamengo' ✓.\n\nEdge: \"Fluminense-RJ\"/\"Fluminense\" → 'fluminense' ✓.\n\nEdge: \"Corinthians-SP\"/\"Corinthians\"/\"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" → [corinthians, paulista]... wait \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" → [sport, club→strip, corinthians, paulista] → 'sport corinthians paulista'?? Hmm! That's the FULL NAME example from the spec: \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\" should → corinthians. My tokens: sport, corinthians, paulista → key 'sport corinthians paulista' ≠ 'corinthians'. Need alias: 'sport corinthians paulista' → 'corinthians'. Also 'corinthians paulista' → 'corinthians'. Add to ALIASES. Similarly \"Sociedade Esportiva Palmeiras\" → [palmeiras] ✓ ('sociedade' not in legals — add 'sociedade'? or it stays 'sociedade esportiva palmeiras' → tokens [sociedade, esportiva→? 'esportiva' in legals, palmeiras] → 'sociedade palmeiras'. Hmm add 'sociedade' to LEGAL_TOKENS → 'palmeiras' ✓.\n\nLet me define LEGAL_TOKENS = {'ec','sc','fc','ac','cb','aa','cbd','ecb','spfc'?no...,'esporte','esportiva','clube','club','futebol','regatas','sociedade','de','do','da','dos','das','the','sporting'?NO,'escolinha'no}. Careful with 'sporting': \"Sporting Cristal\", \"Sporting CP\", \"Sporting Lokeren\" — 'sporting' should NOT be stripped (it's their name). OK.\n\nMore full names: \"Fortaleza Esporte Clube\" (spec mentions) → [fortaleza] ✓. \"Avaí Futebol Clube\"? not present but → [avai] ✓. \"Grêmio Foot-Ball Porto Alegrense\"? not present. \"São Paulo Futebol Clube\" → [sao, paulo] ✓. \"Sport Club do Recife\" → 'sport recife' → alias ✓. \"Club de Regatas Vasco da Gama\"? not present. \"Botafogo de Futebol e Regatas\"? not present. OK.\n\nALIASES also: 'corinthians paulista' → 'corinthians'; 'sport corinthians paulista' → 'corinthians'; 'sociedade palmeiras' handled by adding 'sociedade' to legals.\n\nAlso add: 'atletico clube goianiensis'? skip. 'ac goianiense'? BR-Football might have \"AC Goianiense\"? tokens [goianiense] ✓ fine.\n\nAlso \"Red Bull Bragantino\" ✓; alias 'bragantino' → 'red bull bragantino'? If user types just \"Bragantino\". Add ALIASES['bragantino'] = 'red bull bragantino'. And \"RB Bragantino\"? → [rb, bragantino] — 'rb'? keep → 'rb bragantino' — add alias 'rb bragantino' → 'red bull bragantino'. Hmm wait BR-Football may have \"Red Bull Bragantino\" exactly. Let me not over-add; I'll check the collision report and add what's needed.\n\n### DISPLAY names\n\nDISPLAY = {\n  'flamengo': 'Flamengo', 'fluminense': 'Fluminense', 'vasco': 'Vasco da Gama', 'botafogo': 'Botafogo',\n  'corinthians': 'Corinthians', 'palmeiras': 'Palmeiras', 'sao paulo': 'São Paulo', 'santos': 'Santos',\n  'gremio': 'Grêmio', 'internacional': 'Internacional', 'cruzeiro': 'Cruzeiro', 'atletico-mg': 'Atlético-MG',\n  'athletico-pr': 'Athletico-PR', 'atletico-go': 'Atlético-GO', 'bahia': 'Bahia', 'vitoria': 'Vitória',\n  'sport': 'Sport', 'santa cruz': 'Santa Cruz', 'nautico': 'Náutico', 'ceara': 'Ceará', 'fortaleza': 'Fortaleza',\n  'goias': 'Goiás', 'coritiba': 'Coritiba', 'parana': 'Paraná', 'chapecoense': 'Chapecoense', 'avai': 'Avaí',\n  'figueirense': 'Figueirense', 'criciuma': 'Criciúma', 'juventude': 'Juventude', 'csa': 'CSA',\n  'cuiaba': 'Cuiabá', 'america-mg': 'América-MG', 'america-rn': 'América-RN', 'ponte preta': 'Ponte Preta',\n  'portuguesa': 'Portuguesa', 'red bull bragantino': 'Red Bull Bragantino', 'atletico goianiense'?? \n  'joinville': 'Joinville', 'guarani': 'Guarani', 'paysandu': 'Paysandu', 'sao caetano': 'São Caetano',\n  'brasiliense': 'Brasiliense', 'ipatinga': 'Ipatinga', 'santo andre': 'Santo André', 'barueri': 'Barueri',\n  'gremio prudente': 'Grêmio Prudente', 'botafogo-pb': 'Botafogo-PB', 'botafogo-sp': 'Botafogo-SP',\n}\nFallback: most-common raw variant.\n\n### dates.py\n\nparse_date(s) handles: 'YYYY-MM-DD', 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM', 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS', 'DD/MM/YYYY', 'NA'/'-'/'' → None.\nUse datetime.strptime attempts.\n\n### models.py\n\n```python\n@dataclass(frozen=True? no—slots) class Match:\n    competition: str\n    season: int | None\n    date: dt.date | None\n    time: str | None\n    stage: str | None\n    round_number: int | None\n    home: str  # canonical key\n    away: str\n    home_goals: int | None\n    away_goals: int | None\n    venue: str | None\n    source: str\n    stats: MatchStats | None = None\n\n@dataclass class MatchStats:\n    home_corners, away_corners, home_shots, away_shots, home_attacks, away_attacks: int|None\n    home_ht, away_ht: int|None\n\n@dataclass class Player:\n    player_id, name, age, nationality, overall, potential, club, position, jersey, height, weight, value_eur, preferred_foot, skill ratings dict? \n```\n\nKeep Player with a `skills: dict[str,int]` for a few known attributes (Crossing, Finishing, HeadingAccuracy, ShortPassing, Volleys, Dribbling, Curve, FKAccuracy, LongPassing, BallControl, ShotPower, Penalties, StandingTackle, GKDiving...). I'll include the main skill columns list.\n\nValue parsing: '€110.5M' → 110500000; '€565K' → 565000; '€226.5M' release clause — I'll parse Value and Wage.\n\n### data.py\n\n```python\nclass SoccerData:\n    def __init__(self, data_dir):\n        load everything\n        self.matches: list[Match]  # primary unified\n        self.extended: list[Match with stats]  # BR-Football records (competition canonical)\n        self.players: list[Player]\n        self.teams: dict[key, TeamInfo(display, variants Counter, sources)]\n        self._matches_by_team: defaultdict key→list of (match, side)\n    def resolve_team(self, name) -> key (with fuzzy suggestions)\n```\n\nCompetition mapping for sources:\n- brasileirao_matches → 'Brasileirão Série A'\n- historico → 'Brasileirão Série A'\n- brfootball: 'Serie A' → 'Brasileirão Série A', 'Serie B' → 'Brasileirão Série B', 'Serie C' → 'Brasileirão Série C', 'Copa do Brasil' → 'Copa do Brasil'\n- cup file → 'Copa do Brasil'\n- libertadores file → 'Copa Libertadores'\n\nPrimary source priority (per competition+season, first source with ≥ 60% of that season-competition max? No — simpler fixed order):\n- Série A: ['brasileirao', 'historico', 'brfootball']  — 2003-2011 historico; 2012-2022 brasileirao; 2023 brfootball ✓\n- Série B: ['brfootball']\n- Série C: ['brfootball']\n- Copa do Brasil: ['cup', 'brfootball']  — 2012-2021 cup; 2022-2023 brfootball ✓\n- Libertadores: ['libertadores']\n\nWait — is that right for Serie A? Priority list means: for season 2019, brasileirao has matches → use brasileirao ONLY. For 2005, brasileirao none → historico. For 2023, neither → brfootball. ✓ \n\nBut hold on — what about seasons where the first source has only PARTIAL coverage and a later source is more complete? E.g. Série A 2014: brasileirao 380 ✓ complete. brfootball Serie A 2014: 281 (partial) — skipped ✓ good.\nCopa 2021: cup=108, brf=111 — cup wins by priority (has rounds). Fine.\n\nextended stats: keep ALL BR-Football records in `self.extended` (each a Match with competition label + stats). Also link: for primary matches, attach stats when a matching extended record exists (same competition + season + home + away keys). I'll do a join: build index (competition, season, home, away) → extended record; attach to primary matches (first match). For cups, same pairing may occur twice (two legs in same direction? e.g. cup two legs are usually home-and-away so different directions; but re-matches possible). Join greedily: for each extended record, find primary matches with same comp+season+teams, pick one without stats yet and closest date. Implement simply: index primary by (comp, season, home, away) → list; for each extended record assign to the closest-dated unassigned primary. Fine.\n\nStandings computed from primary Série A matches per season. Note 2003-2004 had 46 matches/round robin? 2003: 552 matches = 24 teams (552 = 24×23) ✓ single round-robin then playoffs? Actually 2003 Brasileirão: 24 teams, 46 rounds (double round robin would be 552). ✓ whatever, standings computed from what's there.\n\nBut caution: points system — 3 points win, 1 draw (since 1995 in Brazil? Yes, 3 points since 1995). ✓\n\nRelegation: bottom 4. For seasons with 20 teams → 4 relegated ✓ (2012-2022: 20 teams, 4 relegated). 2003-2005 had different counts (24 teams → various). I'll mark bottom 4 regardless, noting it matches modern seasons.\n\n### queries.py\n\nFunctions returning plain dicts:\n- search_matches(data, team=None, opponent=None, competition=None, season=None, date_from=None, date_to=None, stage=None, round=None, limit=25, require_result=True?)\n- head_to_head(data, team_a, team_b, competition=None, season=None, limit=None)\n- team_stats(data, team, season=None, competition=None, venue='all')\n- standings(data, competition='Brasileirão Série A', season)\n- relegated(data, competition, season)\n- finals(data, competition, season=None)\n- players(data, name=None, nationality=None, club=None, position=None, min_overall=None, max_overall=None, min_potential=None, limit=20, sort='overall')\n- club_overview(data, club)\n- competition_stats(data, competition, season=None)\n- biggest_wins(data, competition=None, season=None, limit=10)\n- derby_matches(data, derby=None, season=None, competition=None, limit=50)\n- match_stats(data, team=None, opponent=None, competition=None, season=None, limit=20)\n- resolve_team_info(data, name)\n- competitions(data)\n\nTeam resolution & fuzzy: known keys + display names; difflib.get_close_matches. For user input, first try exact normalize; if not in registry, fuzzy match against keys and display names; if still nothing → error with suggestions.\n\nFor player search by club: also resolve club via team registry? FIFA clubs include foreign clubs (\"FC Barcelona\") — resolution for player club should match against FIFA club names directly (substring, case-insensitive), NOT the match-data registry. E.g. club=\"Grêmio\" matches FIFA club \"Grêmio\" ✓; club=\"flamengo\" — no FIFA club... returns empty with helpful message? The spec says \"Which players play for Flamengo? → Filter FIFA data by Club containing 'Flamengo'\" — the expected behavior is a filter, which returns 0 rows for Flamengo (data doesn't have it). I'll implement club filter as substring match on club name (case-insensitive, accent-insensitive). And ALSO if the club matches a Brazilian team in match data, mention that. Keep simple: substring match.\n\nName search: substring, case-insensitive, accent-insensitive. \"Gabriel Barbosa\" → no match in FIFA 19 data (\"Gabriel Jesus\" yes). Hmm — \"Who is Gabriel Barbosa?\" — FIFA 19 dataset (2019 ratings)... does it have Gabriel Barbosa? The Gabriel list printed: Gabriel Jesus, Gabriel Paulista, Gabriel, Gabriel Boschilia, Gabriel Silva, Gabriel Xavier, Gabrielzinho, João Gabriel, Gabriel Nunes... no \"Gabriel Barbosa\". So answer: no exact match; return near matches (other Gabriels). My search_players with name substring 'gabriel barbosa' → 0; I'll auto-fallback: if no results for full-name query, try first name / individual tokens and report close matches. Good UX: return {\"matches\": [], \"note\": \"...\", \"similar\": [...]}. Let me implement: exact substring → if empty, token-level substring (any token) → if empty, difflib on names.\n\nNationality: 'Brazil' → 827 players ✓. club filter for e.g. 'Grêmio' → 20 players.\n\npositions: FIFA positions incl 'ST','GK',... Also \"forwards\" semantics — user says \"forwards from São Paulo FC\" — LLM maps to position values. I'll accept a `position_group` convenience: {'forwards': ST,LS,RS,LW,RW,LF,RF,CF; 'midfielders': CAM,CM,CDM,LM,RM,LAM,LCM,RCM,RDM,LDM,RAM; 'defenders': CB,LCB,RCB,LB,RB,RWB,LWB; 'goalkeepers': GK}. Add param `position_group`. Nice.\n\n### server.py\n\nMCPServer with 14 tools wrapping queries with data loaded at import. Also `if __name__ == '__main__': mcp.run()`.\n\nError handling: each tool catches TeamResolutionError → returns {\"error\": ..., \"suggestions\": [...]}.\n\n### Tests\n\nconftest: session-scoped fixture `soccer` = SoccerData(data dir). \n\nBDD GWT structure: \n\n```python\nclass TestFindMatchesBetweenTwoTeams:\n    def test_returns_matches_with_date_scores_and_competition(self, soccer):\n        \"\"\"Scenario: Find matches between two teams\"\"\"\n        # Given the match data is loaded\n        # When I search for matches between \"Flamengo\" and \"Fluminense\"\n        result = queries.search_matches(soccer, team=\"Flamengo\", opponent=\"Fluminense\")\n        # Then I should receive a list of matches\n        assert result[\"total_matches\"] > 0\n        ...\n```\n\nAssertions grounded in actual data (verified facts):\n- 2019 Brasileirão champion: Flamengo (90 pts — verify from data).\n- 2020 relegated: Coritiba, Vasco, Goiás, Sport (verify).\n- 2018 Copa Libertadores final: Boca Juniors vs River Plate (the famous 2018 final). In lib data: 2018 stage 'final' rows → verify teams: Boca Juniors x River Plate ✓ (I saw 2015 R16 Boca-River with '-' goals — that was the abandoned match!). 2018 final: River won 3-1 extra time. Check data.\n- Palmeiras 2016 champion (70 pts?), verify.\n- Gabriel Jesus in FIFA (Overall 89? position ST? club Manchester City).\n- Neymar Jr: not in FIFA 19? Wait — earlier top Brazilian players sample says Neymar 92. Is Neymar in this FIFA dataset? Nationality counts: Brazil 827. Let me check Neymar, Alisson, Casemiro presence.\n\nLet me verify these facts against the data before writing test assertions. Also verify Fla-Flu h2h counts and Corinthians 2022 home record for the GWT example in the spec (spec example says 19 matches — 2022 Brasileirão Corinthians home: 19 home matches ✓ but W/D/L from data).\n\nAlso test_mcp_server: spawn server.py subprocess via stdio_client + ClientSession, initialize, list tools (expect 14), call search_matches, get_standings, search_players. Must ensure server imports fast. Data load ~1-2s — ok. Use session-scoped fixture for the server process (expensive). anyio/asyncio: pytest needs anyio plugin or asyncio marker — pytest doesn't have asyncio plugin installed (no pytest-asyncio!). I can use `anyio.pytest_plugin`? anyio provides a pytest plugin (`anyio_backend` fixture) — anyio IS installed as mcp dep. `import anyio` + `@pytest.fixture def anyio_backend(): return 'asyncio'`. anyio's pytest plugin is auto-loaded via entrypoint? anyio ships `anyio.pytest_plugin` registered via entry points ✓ (pytest plugin autoload). I'll use `@pytest.mark.anyio` tests... The anyio pytest plugin requires the `anyio_backend` fixture. Let me verify it's registered: `pytest --co` with a trivial async test. I'll test that during the run. Alternative: run asyncio.run() inside a sync test — simplest, zero plugin dependency:\n\n```python\ndef test_tools_list():\n    async def scenario():\n        async with Client(StdioServerParameters(...)) as client:\n            ...\n    asyncio.run(scenario())\n```\n\nClean, no plugin needed. I'll do that.\n\nAlso unit tests run fast: data load once per session via conftest fixture.\n\nTiming test: spec performance criteria — simple lookups < 2s, aggregates < 5s. Add a performance test measuring in-memory query latency (loosely, e.g. < 2s) to encode the criteria. \n\nNow — verify facts. Let me run quick checks: 2019 standings from data (champion + points), 2020 bottom 4, 2018 Libertadores final teams, Neymar/Alisson/Casemiro/Gabriel Jesus in FIFA, Corinthians 2022 home record, Fla-Flu h2h totals. Also count total primary matches for stats sanity (~?).\n\nI'll write the implementation first, then run these checks using it. Actually — write modules now, then a scratch verification script, then tests with verified numbers.\n\nOne more design point — the `Player` value/height parsing: keep raw + parsed numeric (value_eur). Height \"5'7\" (feets'inches), weight \"159lbs\" — keep raw strings.\n\nLet me also think about `search_matches` result shape:\n\n```python\n{\n  \"query\": {...echo filters...},\n  \"total_matches\": int,      # full count\n  \"returned\": int,\n  \"truncated\": bool,\n  \"matches\": [\n     {\"date\": \"2023-09-03\", \"time\": \"16:00\", \"competition\": \"Brasileirão Série A\", \"season\": 2023,\n      \"stage\": null, \"round\": 22, \"home\": \"Flamengo\", \"away\": \"Fluminense\",\n      \"score\": \"2-1\", \"home_goals\": 2, \"away_goals\": 1, \"result\": \"home_win\",\n      \"venue\": \"Maracanã\"?, \"source\": \"brasileirao_matches\", \"stats\": {...}|null}\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"17 matches found...\"?\n}\n```\n\nSorting: date desc (most recent first) — good default. Add `order` param? Keep date desc; LLM can handle.\n\nh2h shape:\n```python\n{\"team_a\": \"Flamengo\", \"team_b\": \"Fluminense\",\n \"matches\": [...], \"total_matches\": n,\n \"record\": {\"team_a_wins\": x, \"team_b_wins\": y, \"draws\": z},\n \"goals\": {\"team_a\": g, \"team_b\": g},\n \"latest\": {...}, \"biggest_home_win\"?...}\n```\n\nteam_stats shape:\n```python\n{\"team\": \"Corinthians\", \"season\": 2022, \"competition\": null/\"Brasileirão Série A\", \"venue\": \"home\",\n \"record\": {\"matches\",\"wins\",\"draws\",\"losses\",\"goals_for\",\"goals_against\",\"win_rate\"},\n \"by_competition\": [ {competition, matches, W/D/L, GF, GA} ... ] (when competition not specified),\n \"by_season\": [...] (when season not specified),\n \"recent_form\": last 5?  — nice extra: \"last_5\": [\"W\",\"D\",...]}\n```\n\nstandings shape:\n```python\n{\"competition\": ..., \"season\": ...,\n \"table\": [{\"position\", \"team\", \"matches\", \"wins\",\"draws\",\"losses\",\"goals_for\",\"goals_against\",\"goal_diff\",\"points\"}...],\n \"champion\": \"Flamengo\",\n \"relegated\": [bottom 4],\n \"note\": \"calculated from matches in ... source\"}\n```\n\ncompetition_stats:\n```python\n{\"competition\",\"season\",\"matches\",\"goals_total\",\"avg_goals_per_match\",\"home_wins\",\"away_wins\",\"draws\",\"home_win_rate\",\"draw_rate\",\"away_win_rate\",\"avg_home_goals\",\"avg_away_goals\",\"biggest_win\": {...}}\n```\n\nplayers:\n```python\n{\"filters\": {...}, \"total_matches\"? -> \"total\": n, \"returned\": n, \"truncated\": bool,\n \"players\": [{\"id\",\"name\",\"age\",\"nationality\",\"overall\",\"potential\",\"club\",\"position\",\"jersey_number\",\"value\",\"skills\":{...}}]}\n```\n\nclub_overview:\n```python\n{\"club\": \"Grêmio\", \"team_stats_summary\": {...overall record...}, \"squad\": {\"count\": 20, \"avg_overall\": 74, \"top_players\":[...]}, \"competitions_played\": [...]}\n```\n\nderby_matches:\n```python\n{\"derby\": \"Fla-Flu\", \"teams\": [\"Flamengo\",\"Fluminense\"], \"matches\": [...], \"record\": {...}}\n# or when derby=None: {\"derbies\": [{\"name\",\"teams\"}...], \"matches\": [...] for all rivalry pairs}\n```\n\nmatch_stats (extended):\n```python\n{\"matches\": [{\"date\",\"competition\",\"season\",\"home\",\"away\",\"score\",\"corners\":{\"home\",\"away\"},\"shots\":{...},\"attacks\":{...},\"half_time\":\"1-0\"}]}\n```\n\nfind_finals:\n```python\n{\"competition\": \"Copa Libertadores\", \"finals\": [{\"season\", \"matches\": [...], \"winner\": ...}]}\n```\n\nNote on Copa do Brasil finals via max round; Libertadores via stage='final' (with the NA-season 2022 final having no season — season None. I'll include with season from... it has 'NA' season — keep None and note date? The row: datetime NA, Flamengo home, Athletico away, goals '-', stage final. So it has no date/goals either. Winner None. Include as an entry with mostly nulls? It's the only 'final' with unknown season. I'll include seasons sorted with None last. Also for winner determination: two-legged finals (Libertadores finals 2013-2019 were two legs; stage='final' 15 matches over 2013-2022). Determining overall winner from two legs needs aggregate — doable: group final matches by season, sum goals, pick winner. If tie → report as tie (can't break by away goals reliably... Libertadores used away goals until 2021ish, then no. I'll compute aggregate and if level, mark \"tie on aggregate (decided on penalties/away goals — not in data)\"). For the 2015 Boca-River R16 '-' goals — that's round of 16, excluded from finals.\n\nWait — 2022 Libertadores final in data is the NA row (Flamengo x Athletico, no goals). And are there TWO 2022 final legs? 2022 final was single match. So finals list: 2013 (2 legs), ..., 2019, 2021 (single match? 2021 final Palmeiras x Flamengo single match in Montevideo), 2022 NA row. Winner for 2021: Palmeiras (1-0, extra time). For NA 2022: goals missing → winner None (note). Hmm — actually wait, let me look at the 'final' rows to be sure of the structure before finalizing winner logic. 15 'final' matches. Let me list them during verification.\n\nOK. Enough planning — write the code now. After code, run collision report + facts verification, then adjust aliases, then write tests, then run everything.\n\nrequirements.txt:\n```\nmcp>=2.1,<3\n```\n(dev: pytest, pytest-cov already in venv; note in README.)\n\nNow write the files.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d995332001wWM4JKADEBt6Zi","sessionID":"ses_fa26ff80dffeDQKLW66czjBP2c","messageID":"msg_05d9803940017XcvUYJNXpjx0Q"}}
