       chosen = self._choose_primary_sources(raw_by_source)\n        for match in chosen:\n            self._add_match(match)"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bg7g52hu/retort-7ef2ffebd247/brazilian_soccer/data.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bg7g52hu/retort-7ef2ffebd247/brazilian_soccer/data.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bg7g52hu/retort-7ef2ffebd247/brazilian_soccer/data.py\n@@ -133,16 +133,11 @@\n for match in self._load_brazilian_cup():\n     raw_by_source[\"brazilian_cup\"].append(match)\n for match in self._load_libertadores():\n     raw_by_source[\"libertadores\"].append(match)\n-for match in self._load_br_football(primary=False):\n+for match in self._load_br_football():\n     raw_by_source[\"br_football\"].append(match)\n \n-for source, matches in raw_by_source.items():\n-    for match in matches:\n-        self._register_team(match.home, match.source)\n-        self._register_team(match.away, match.source)\n-\n chosen = self._choose_primary_sources(raw_by_source)\n for match in chosen:\n     self._add_match(match)\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bg7g52hu/retort-7ef2ffebd247/brazilian_soccer/data.py","patch":"Index: /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bg7g52hu/retort-7ef2ffebd247/brazilian_soccer/data.py\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bg7g52hu/retort-7ef2ffebd247/brazilian_soccer/data.py\n+++ /Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-bg7g52hu/retort-7ef2ffebd247/brazilian_soccer/data.py\n@@ -133,16 +133,11 @@\n for match in self._load_brazilian_cup():\n     raw_by_source[\"brazilian_cup\"].append(match)\n for match in self._load_libertadores():\n     raw_by_source[\"libertadores\"].append(match)\n-for match in self._load_br_football(primary=False):\n+for match in self._load_br_football():\n     raw_by_source[\"br_football\"].append(match)\n \n-for source, matches in raw_by_source.items():\n-    for match in matches:\n-        self._register_team(match.home, match.source)\n-        self._register_team(match.away, match.source)\n-\n chosen = self._choose_primary_sources(raw_by_source)\n for match in chosen:\n     self._add_match(match)\n \n","additions":1,"deletions":6},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/data.py","time":{"start":1788277011162,"end":1788277011165}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait, there's a bug in `_load_brasileirao_matches` — the time parsing: `str(row[\"datetime\"]).split(\" \")[1] if \" \" in str(row.get(\"datetime\", \"\"))` — if datetime is \"2012-05-19 18:30:00\" → time \"18:30:00\" ✓; \"NA\" → None ✓. OK.\n\nBut there's a subtlety in `_choose_primary_sources`: the logic — for each match, get the pool of sources for its (competition, season). If this match's source is not the minimum-priority source present in pool → skip. That means: keep matches only from the single best-priority source available for that season. My condition: `if pool and priority.index(source) < min(priority.index(s) for s in pool if s in priority): continue` — wait that skips when source priority index is LOWER (better) than the best in pool?? That's backwards! If source is better (lower index) than min, we should KEEP. Let me redo:\n\nbest = min(priority.index(s) for s in pool if s in priority) — the priority index of the best source in pool.\nSkip if priority.index(source) > best (worse than best).\n\nMy condition skips if index(source) < best — wrong direction. Also `priority.index(source)` will raise ValueError if source not in priority list (e.g., competition not in SOURCE_PRIORITY). Need safe handling.\n\nLet me fix:\n\n```python\ndef _choose_primary_sources(raw_by_source):\n    covered: dict[(comp, season), set[str]] = defaultdict(set)\n    for source, matches in raw_by_source.items():\n        for match in matches:\n            covered[(match.competition, match.season)].add(source)\n    def best_rank(pool):\n        ranks = [priority.index(s) for s in pool if s in priority]  # if source not in priority?\n        return min(ranks) if ranks else len(priority) + 1?? \n```\n\nHmm, sources not listed in the competition's priority (shouldn't happen since priority covers all sources per competition: serie a: all 3, serie b/c: br_football, copa: 2, libertadores: lib). But BR-Football could have unexpected tournament names mapped via BR_FOOTBALL_COMPETITIONS.get(row['tournament'], row['tournament']) — an unknown tournament string would produce a competition with no priority list. Then priority = SOURCE_PRIORITY.get(comp) → None → handle: treat source as rank +inf (keep, it's the only source for unknown competition) — but if unknown competition comes only from br_football, pool={br_football}, all sources equal rank → keep. General rule: for sources not in priority list, assign rank = big number so they lose only to listed ones... but if ONLY unlisted sources exist in a pool, everything ties and all are kept. Fine.\n\nActually, let me simplify with an explicit chosen-source map:\n\n```python\ndef _choose_primary_sources(raw_by_source):\n    seasons = {}  # (comp, season) -> set of sources\n    for source, matches in raw_by_source.items():\n        for m in matches:\n            seasons.setdefault((m.competition, m.season), set()).add(source)\n    primary = {}\n    for key_, pool in seasons.items():\n        comp = key_[0]\n        priority = SOURCE_PRIORITY.get(comp, [])\n        ranked = [s for s in priority if s in pool] or sorted(pool)\n        primary[key_] = set(ranked[:1])\n    chosen = [m for source, matches in raw_by_source.items() for m in matches if source in primary[(m.competition, m.season)]]\n    chosen.sort(...)\n```\n\nClean. Note: if a season has sources {'brasileirao_matches', 'historico', 'br_football'} for Serie A → ranked = ['brasileirao_matches'] (first in priority present in pool). ✓\n\nLet me also double check the `_load_br_football(primary=False)` — the `primary` param is unused; remove it. Also season from date[:4] — for BR-Football all dates present ✓.\n\nOne issue in `_attach_extended_stats`: `min(candidates, key=lambda c: (c[0], c[1]))` — candidates tuples are (days, i, m); min by (days, index) ✓. But id() used in `used` set — fine.\n\nAlso in `_load_brasileirao_matches` I call `_register_team(match.home, match.source, raw_home)` — this happens inside loaders BEFORE `_load_all` registers again? In `_load_all` I ALSO loop `for match in raw...: self._register_team(match.home, match.source)` — duplicate registration without raw (harmless, just adds source again). But actually the loaders already register with raw variants, so the loop in `_load_all` is redundant. Remove it.\n\nAlso, the time parsing for Brazilian cup: `datetime` \"2012-03-07 16:00:00\" ✓.\n\nAlso `_register_team` signature: (key, source, raw) — in `_load_all` I called `self._register_team(match.home, match.source)` without raw — removing that loop entirely.\n\nLet me rewrite data.py with these fixes.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d9da8ba001GmWrgSZ7czdoeG","sessionID":"ses_fa26ff80dffeDQKLW66czjBP2c","messageID":"msg_05d9c2284001pVaMk2LwcyIbTa"}}
