.date.min` — ugly. Import datetime at top: `import datetime as dt` and use `dt.date.min`.\n2. In `search_matches`, the closure capture of `team_key_`/`opp_key` in lambdas — fine since they're local vars not loop vars.\n3. `find_finals`: `decisive = decisive` — pointless line. Remove.\n4. In `find_finals` winner determination: `totals[m.home] += m.home_goals` — two-legged finals aggregate. OK. But `winner_on_aggregate` expression: `data.teams[next(iter(set(leaders)))].display` — leaders is already a list of display names! Bug: `totals` keys are team KEYS; leaders = display names. Then `data.teams[next(iter(set(leaders)))]` — indexing with a display name — KeyError. Fix: leaders should be keys, then convert.\n5. In `head_to_head` — when `team_a == key_b` etc. fine. Also `record` keys use display names with spaces — `{f\"{display}_wins\": ...}` produces e.g. \"Flamengo_wins\". JSON keys with underscores fine.\n6. `search_players` — `payload[\"note\"]` logic: `if not result and name and not folded_name:` — folded_name is truthy if name given; that branch is dead. Simplify: if not result and name: similar.\n7. `club_overview` — club match in FIFA: `folded_club in fold_text(player.club)` — \"santos\" in \"Santos Laguna\"?? That would match Mexican Santos Laguna! Substring too loose. Better: exact folded match OR contained — hmm. For \"Santos\" exact match is right; for \"Grêmio\" exact. For \"São Paulo\" exact. But FIFA club names like \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\"... resolved club is america-mg, display \"América-MG\" — folded \"america-mg\" won't substring-match \"america fc (minas gerais)\". Hmm. Cross-file club matching needs the alias structure: match FIFA club names by resolving them via team_key! I can resolve the FIFA club string through team_key and compare to the team key. \"Santos Laguna\" → key \"santos laguna\" ≠ \"santos\" ✓. \"Santos\" → \"santos\" ✓. \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" → \"america\" → BARE_DEFAULTS → \"america-mg\" ✓!! \"Atlético Paranaense\" → \"athletico-pr\" ✓. \"Sport Club do Recife\" → \"sport recife\" → alias → \"sport\" ✓. \"Grêmio\" → \"gremio\" ✓. \"Atlético Madrid\" → \"atletico madrid\" ≠ \"atletico-mg\" ✓ good. \"Botafogo\" → \"botafogo\" ✓. \"Vitória\" → \"vitoria\" ✓ (Vitória Guimarães → \"vitoria guimaraes\" ✓ distinct). \n\n   So: squad = [p for p in players if p.club and team_key(p.club) == key]. But careful: FIFA club \"São Paulo\"? Not in FIFA (no Flamengo/Palmeiras/SPFC/Corinthians). Fine.\n   \n   Edge: FIFA \"Bahia\" → \"bahia\" ✓ matches. FIFA \"Cruzeiro\" ✓. FIFA \"Internacional\" ✓. FIFA \"Chapecoense\" ✓. FIFA \"Paraná\" → \"parana\" ✓. FIFA \"Ceará Sporting Club\" → \"ceara sporting\" → ALIASES → \"ceara\" ✓!! \n\n   So use team_key comparison. Also allow fallback to exact display-name match. Implement: `squad = [p for p in data.players if p.club and (team_key(p.club) == key or fold_text(p.club) == folded_club)]`.\n\n8. `standings` — relegation bottom 4: for seasons with 24 teams (2003) it's \"bottom 4\" regardless; fine, documented.\n\n9. `biggest_wins` — fine.\n\n10. `search_match_stats` — note `pool` filtered by `m.stats is not None` via conditions already; the `[m for m in pool if m.stats]` redundant but harmless.\n\n11. `_resolve_team` — data.resolve_team raises TeamResolutionError with suggestions from display names — good.\n\n12. Unused imports: `FIFA_SKILL_COLUMNS`, `Counter` (used in find_finals ✓), `parse_date` used ✓, `SERIE_B`/`SERIE_C` used ✓. Remove FIFA_SKILL_COLUMNS import if unused — yes unused. Remove.\n\n13. `best_players_by_nationality` — search_players(nationality=...) ✓.\n\nAlso `head_to_head` conditions when comp/season None: `_pick([cond], matches)` where cond uses comp... fine.\n\nOne more: in `search_matches`, sorting by date desc — `m.date or dt.date.min` reverse=True → None dates last. ✓\n\nLet me fix these issues.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05da034650011BHjQFFiIz7ULU","sessionID":"ses_fa26ff80dffeDQKLW66czjBP2c","messageID":"msg_05d9f