: \"botafogo-pb\", \"SP\": \"botafogo-sp\"},\n    \"central\": {\"PE\": \"central\", \"SC\": \"central-sc\"},\n    \"comercial\": {\"MS\": \"comercial-ms\", \"PI\": \"comercial-pi\"},\n    \"flamengo\": {\"RJ\": \"flamengo\", \"PI\": \"flamengo-pi\"},\n    \"fluminense\": {\"RJ\": \"fluminense\", \"PI\": \"fluminense-pi\"},\n    \"guarani\": {\"SP\": \"guarani\", \"CE\": \"guarani-ce\"},\n    \"internacional\": {\"RS\": \"internacional\", \"SC\": \"internacional-sc\"},\n    \"juventude\": {\"RS\": \"juventude\", \"MA\": \"juventude-ma\"},\n    \"nautico\": {\"PE\": \"nautico\", \"RR\": \"nautico-rr\"},\n    \"operario\": {\"PR\": \"operario-pr\", \"MS\": \"operario-ms\", \"MT\": \"operario-mt\"},\n    \"portuguesa\": {\"SP\": \"portuguesa\", \"RJ\": \"portuguesa-rj\"},\n    \"rio branco\": {\"AC\": \"rio branco-ac\", \"ES\": \"rio branco-es\"},\n    \"river\": {\"PI\": \"river-pi\", \"AC\": \"river-ac\"},\n    \"santa cruz\": {\"PE\": \"santa cruz\", \"RN\": \"santa cruz-rn\", \"RS\": \"santa cruz-rs\"},\n    \"santos\": {\"SP\": \"santos\", \"AP\": \"santos-ap\"},\n    \"sao francisco\": {\"PA\": \"sao francisco-pa\", \"AC\": \"sao francisco-ac\"},\n    \"sao jose\": {\"RS\": \"sao jose-rs\", \"PA\": \"sao jose-pa\"},\n    \"sao raimundo\": {\"PA\": \"sao raimundo-pa\", \"AM\": \"sao raimundo-am\", \"RR\": \"sao raimundo-rr\"},\n    \"vitoria\": {\"BA\": \"vitoria\", \"ES\": \"vitoria-es\"},\n    \"ypiranga\": {\"RS\": \"ypiranga-rs\", \"AP\": \"ypiranga-ap\"},\n    \"bragantino\": {\"SP\": \"red bull bragantino\", \"PA\": \"bragantino-pa\"},\n}\n```\n\nAnd BARE_DEFAULTS (for names without any suffix — these map to the famous club):\n- america → america-mg\n- athletico → athletico-pr\n- botafogo → botafogo (RJ) — identity, but keep explicit\n- bragantino → red bull bragantino\n- flamengo → flamengo (identity)\n- fluminense, santos, guarani, portuguesa, internacional, juventude, nautico, santa cruz, vitoria, operario? — bare operario → ? which one... \"Operário\" bare appears? In variants above: 'Operario PR' etc. all have suffix. Bare 'Operário'? not seen. If bare appears, no default → keep 'operario' key (its own identity, separate from the -pr/-ms/-mt ones — slight orphan but OK).\n- central bare? 'Central SC' only. 'central' bare? no.\n- comercial bare? no ('Comercial MS' etc.).\n- rio branco bare? no.\n- river bare? no.\n- sao jose/sao raimundo/sao francisco/ypiranga bare? 'Ypiranga' bare appears! (in variants: 'Ypiranga' without suffix). Bare ypiranga → default? Hmm, which Ypiranga is bare 'Ypiranga'? If it's from BR-Football Serie C... could be either AP or RS. Leave as own key 'ypiranga' (orphan, fine).\n- 'Santa Cruz FC' (bare) → santa cruz (PE) default ✓ (Santa Cruz FC is the PE club).\n- 'Náutico' bare (historical, PE) → nautico (PE) default ✓.\n- 'Vitoria'/'Vitória' bare (FIFA + historical BA) → vitoria (BA) ✓.\n- 'Portuguesa' bare (historical SP) → portuguesa (SP) ✓.\n- 'Guarani' bare (historical SP) → guarani (SP) ✓.\n- 'Santos' bare → santos (SP) ✓.\n- 'Flamengo' bare → RJ ✓. 'Fluminense' bare → RJ ✓.\n- 'Internacional' bare → RS ✓.\n- 'Juventude' bare → RS ✓.\n- 'EC Juventude' → bare juventude ✓. 'EC Internacional SC' → SC → internacional-sc ✓.\n\nSo BARE_DEFAULTS:\n```python\n{\n    \"america\": \"america-mg\",\n    \"athletico\": \"athletico-pr\",\n    \"botafogo\": \"botafogo\",\n    \"bragantino\": \"red bull bragantino\",\n    \"flamengo\": \"flamengo\",\n    \"fluminense\": \"fluminense\",\n    \"guarani\": \"guarani\",\n    \"internacional\": \"internacional\",\n    \"juventude\": \"juventude\",\n    \"nautico\": \"nautico\",\n    \"portuguesa\": \"portuguesa\",\n    \"santa cruz\": \"santa cruz\",\n    \"santos\": \"santos\",\n    \"vitoria\": \"vitoria\",\n}\n```\n(Entries identical to base are redundant but explicit; actually for bases where default == base I can omit. But harmless to keep.)\n\nWait — with the new AMBIGUOUS_BASES scheme, there's a subtlety: previously unambiguous bases DROP their UF. Now 'flamengo' is ambiguous → \"Flamengo-RJ\" → AMBIGUOUS['flamengo']['RJ'] = 'flamengo' ✓ and \"Flamengo-PI\" → 'flamengo-pi' ✓. Bare \"Flamengo\" → BARE_DEFAULTS → 'flamengo' ✓. \n\nBut CAREFUL: 'sport' — \"Sport-PE\" → base 'sport' — currently unambiguous → 'sport'. Is there another 'sport' club? \"Sport Boys\" is different base. ✓ stays.\n\n'ceara' ✓. 'bahia' — \"Bahia-BA\" ✓ unambiguous... but wait — is there \"Bahia-PI\"? No. ✓.\n\nAlso 'parana' — \"Paraná-PR\" → 'parana' ✓ (FIFA Paraná too ✓).\n\n'mogi mirim'? whatever, uniques fine.\n\nAlso what about keys that had 2-5 variants but same suffix — fine.\n\nNow the ALIASES 'bragantino' entry must move to BARE_DEFAULTS (since 'bragantino' is now AMBIGUOUS, ALIASES never reached for it — resolution order checks AMBIGUOUS first). Also 'rb bragantino' alias stays.\n\nAdditional check needed — keys where variants include both a bare form matching a DIFFERENT club than the suffixed default... e.g. 'vitoria': bare 'Vitória' from FIFA = Vitória-BA ✓ default BA ✓ correct.\n\nOne more thing: 'santos' — bare \"Santos\" from FIFA = Santos-SP ✓ and \"Santos-AP\" separate ✓. And \"Santos Laguna\" → 'santos laguna' ✓ distinct.\n\nAlso 'nacional': \"Nacional (PAR)\"/\"Nacional-URU\" → country codes → nacional-par/nacional-uru ✓; but there's also \"Atlético Nacional\" → 'atletico nacional' ✓ distinct.\n\nNow update normalize.py with the expanded tables, then re-run collision report and also verify no regressions on the famous clubs. Then also fix facts verification.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05da4d2c6001S1zZ9J3kXmxCLz","sessionID":"ses_fa26ff80dffeDQKLW66czjBP2c","messageID":"msg_05da31716001IMI6e2PyU30rtC"}}
