   folded = fold_text(query)\n+    return _STAGE_ALIASES.get(folded, folded)\n+\n+\n # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n # Shared helpers\n # --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n \n","additions":25,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer/queries.py","time":{"start":1788278088954,"end":1788278088956}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Confirmed:\n- 2015 final: Santos 1-0 Palmeiras, Palmeiras 2-1 Santos → aggregate 3-2 Palmeiras — wait: Palmeiras scored 2+0? Santos goals: 1+1=2; Palmeiras: 0+2=2. AGGREGATE TIE 2-2 (real: Palmeiras won on penalties). My winner=None + note ✓ correct!\n- 2017: Flamengo 1-1, 0-0 → aggregate 1-1 tie (real: Flamengo won on... hmm, actually the 2017 Copa do Brasil final was Flamengo 3-1 agg? No wait — the real 2017 final: Cruzeiro beat Flamengo? Let me recall: 2017 Copa do Brasil champion = Flamengo? No — 2017 Copa do Brasil: Flamengo beat Cruzeiro (1-1, 1-0?)... hmm the data says Flamengo 1-1 Cruzeiro, Cruzeiro 0-0 Flamengo → 1-1 aggregate. Reality: the 2017 Copa do Brasil final was Flamengo vs Cruzeiro, Flamengo won on penalties. YES — Flamengo won 2017 Copa do Brasil on penalties after 1-1 aggregate. So my tie-note is CORRECT ✓.\n- 2018: Cruzeiro 1-0 Corinthians, Corinthians 1-2 Cruzeiro → Cruzeiro 3-1 ✓ (Cruzeiro won 2018 ✓).\n- 2021: max round 4 with 16 matches and NA goals — the file truncates mid-tournament (these are unplayed listed fixtures). Definitely shouldn't be labeled \"final\".\n\nFixes:\n1. `find_finals` for Copa do Brasil: only treat max-round as final if ≤ 2 matches; otherwise add note entry that the final isn't in the data.\n2. Stage filter: exact-match with alias map.\n\nAlso in find_finals for Libertadores — 2013 winner None (2013: Boca? no — 2013 Libertadores champion: Atlético Mineiro beat Olimpia 2-0 after 0-2 (aggregate 2-2 — won on penalties!). So 2013 None + tie note ✓ CORRECT!). 2020 Palmeiras ✓. NA season final (Flamengo-Athletico 2022, no scores) → note ✓.\n\nNow implement the stage fix in search_matches:\n\n```python\n_STAGE_ALIASES = {\n    'final': 'final', 'finals': 'final', 'the final': 'final',\n    'semi': 'semifinals', 'semifinal': 'semifinals', 'semifinals': 'semifinals',\n    'quarter': 'quarterfinals', 'quarterfinal': 'quarterfinals', 'quarterfinals': 'quarterfinals',\n    'quartas': 'quarterfinals',\n    'round of 16': 'round of 16', 'last 16': 'round of 16', '16 avos': ...,\n    'group': 'group stage', 'groups': 'group stage', 'group stage': 'group stage', 'fase de grupos': 'group stage',\n    'oitavas': 'round of 16', 'semis': 'semifinals',\n}\n```\nFilter: m.stage == canonical if resolved; else exact folded equality.\n\nAnd find_finals Copa do Brasil change:\n\n```python\nmax_round = max(...)\ndecisive = [m in max_round]\nif len(decisive) > 2:\n    # not a final — the dataset ends before the final\n    finals.append({\"season\": season_key, \"finals\": [], \"note\": f\"Copa do Brasil {season} data ends at round {max_round} ({len(decisive)} matches); the final is not in the dataset.\"})\n    continue\n```\n\nLet me implement both fixes now","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05dae1e740016VzjDnnV7afjRz","sessionID":"ses_fa26ff80dffeDQKLW66czjBP2c","messageID":"msg_05dadac390012bqTcAufmCkimt"}}
