xpected behavior IS substring. I'll adjust the test to match spec semantics: clubs containing \"Santos\". But that's weird for user Q&A... Better: keep substring behavior (spec-compliant) but make the test assert the documented behavior: every returned club CONTAINS \"santos\" (case-insensitive), and the total is 9 (both Santos + Santos Laguna players?). Hmm — earlier total was 9 with those listed including 'Luimo Boas Santos' — the earlier query returned total 9 with limit 50... but the club mismatch happened only in `p[\"club\"] == \"Santos\"` check. Earlier list showed 9 players, first was 'Luimo Boas Santos' — the name doesn't imply club. Let me see which clubs appear. If \"Santos Laguna\" forwards are included, total 9 includes them.\n\n   Actually — for a BETTER product: exact-match clubs first, then substring? The spec explicitly documents substring behavior, and cross-file queries (club='Grêmio') worked with 20 exact. I'll keep substring but make it smarter: match if folded club EQUALS query OR contains it (substring) — that's what it does. The failure just means results include Santos Laguna. To honor the spec's example (\"Which players play for Flamengo\" → club containing), keep substring; fix the test to assert containment (which IS the spec behavior) and adjust count if needed.\n\n   Let me check what clubs match 'santos' substring in FIFA: 'Santos', 'Santos Laguna', 'Santos FC' (South Africa?), maybe 'Botafogo SP'... no. Let me run and see.\n\n4. Palmeiras 2019 = 52 (fix test).\n5. Palmeiras 2023 match stats = 37 (fix test).\n\nFix the dt import first — check current imports in queries.py.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05dbe5e98001QtHzVIKPVu59WA","sessionID":"ses_fa26ff80dffeDQKLW66czjBP2c","messageID":"msg_05dbd05bf001KfY53o6U1kNCVg"}}
